17In📍 the👆 same💯 way🛣️, faith🙏 without🚫 action💪 is💀 dead💀.
18Someone👤 might💭 say🗣️, “You🫵 have💯 faith🙏; I👤 have💪 actions💪.” Show👀 me👤 faith🙏 without🚫 actions💪, and➡️ I👤 will🔜 show👀 you🫵 my👥 faith🙏 through➡️ what➡️ I👤 do💪—Glaube🇩🇪, emunah✡️.
19You🫵 believe🙏 there💯 is💯 one☝️ God👑? Good💯! Even⚡ demons😈 believe🙏 that👆, and➡️ they🫂 tremble🫨.
20Do💭 you🫵 need💭 proof🔎, you🫵 empty🫙 thinker🧠, that➡️ faith🙏 without🚫 action💪 is💀 dead💀?
21Wasn’t❓ Abraham👴 our👥 ancestor👴 shown👀 righteous⚖️ by🙏 what➡️ he👤 did💪 when⏱️ he👤 offered🎁 Isaac👤 his👥 son👦 on📍 the👑 altar🙏?
22You🫵 see👀 his👤 faith🙏 and➡️ actions💪 working🤝 together🫂; his👤 actions💪 brought🏁 his👤 faith🙏 to➡️ completion✅.
23That👆 fulfilled✅ Scripture📜: “Abraham👴 trusted🙏 God👑, and➡️ God👑 counted🧮 it🫵 as➡️ righteousness⚖️.” Abraham👴 was💯 called📣 God’s👑 friend🫶.
24So➡️ a👤 person👤 is💯 shown👀 righteous⚖️ by🙏 actions💪, not🚫 by🙏 faith🙏 alone☝️—obras🇪🇸, ọrụ🟩.
25Rahab👤 was💯 also💯 shown👀 righteous⚖️ by🙏 what➡️ she👤 did💪 when⏱️ she👤 welcomed🏠 the🕵️ messengers🕵️ and➡️ sent📨 them🫂 out⬆️ by🙏 another🔀 route🛣️.
26As💥 a🫂 body🫂 without🚫 a🌬️ spirit🌬️ is💀 dead💀, faith🙏 without🚫 action💪 is💀 dead💀 too💯—unu🇯🇲.